<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair says no plans for Sabena pullout.</title>
<headline>Swissair says no plans for Sabena pullout.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swissair AG has no plans for pulling out of airline Sabena even if decides to write-off its stake in the Belgian carrier, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not considering pulling out,&quot; spokesman Peter Gutknecht told Reuters.  </p>
<p>In Zurich, Swissair spokesman Gutknecht said the chance of a write-off depended on progress in Sabena's talks with the unions on a recovery deal.</p>
<p>Gutknecht estimated the value of Swissair's 49.5 percent stake in Sabena at about 250 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>Asked about chances Swissair could sell the stake, he said: &quot;That is speculation. It is too early to talk about possible scenarios.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
